#===============================================================================
# @TYPE:       s1-tddft-opt
# @FUNCTIONAL: B3LYP (via LibXC Functional 106)
# @BASIS:      6-31G(d)
# @SOLVENT:    CPCM(Methanol)
# @ORCA:       6.1.0 (libXC 7.0.0)
# @CHARGE:     1
# @MULT:       1
# @SYSTEM:     closed-shell organic chromophore (C22-C26)
# @VERIFIED:   FAILED — see full failure log below. Use CAM-B3LYP instead.
#===============================================================================
# TEMPLATE STATUS: DEPRECATED — DO NOT USE FOR NEW CALCULATIONS
# Recommended alternative: s1_tddft_opt_camb3lyp_631gd.inp
#===============================================================================
#
# ===== COMPLETE FAILURE LOG (2026-05-08) =====
#
# 7 attempts were made to run B3LYP S₁ TD-DFT Opt with LSH-33 in ORCA 6.1.
# All failed. Here is the full diagnostic chain:
#
# ATTEMPT 1: "! TD-DFT Opt B3LYP ..."
#   → INPUT ERROR: UNRECOGNIZED KEYWORD "TD-DFT" in simple input line
#
# ATTEMPT 2: "! TDDFT Opt B3LYP ..." (no hyphen)
#   → INPUT ERROR: UNRECOGNIZED KEYWORD "TDDFT" in simple input line
#
# ATTEMPT 3: "! Opt B3LYP ..." with %tddft block (native B3LYP)
#   → WARNING: Third functional derivative of B88 not available natively
#   → ORCA aborts silently after the warning
#
# ATTEMPT 4: "! Opt PBE ..." + %method Functional 106 (LibXC B3LYP via decoy)
#   → Input accepted, SCF converges, TD-DFT runs
#   → 8 optimization cycles completed
#   → BUT: D3BJ parameters loaded are for PBE (s8=0.7875), not B3LYP (s8=1.9889)
#   → Dispersion correction is WRONG for B3LYP
#
# ATTEMPT 5: %method Functional 106 + %scf UseLibXC true
#   → "UseLibXC" is not recognized in %scf block → error
#
# ATTEMPT 6: %method Functional 106 + D3s6/s8/a1/a2 override
#   → D3s6/s8/a1/a2 keywords cause ORCA CIS module to crash with SIGABRT
#   → These keywords are NOT valid in ORCA 6.1 %method block
#
# ATTEMPT 7: "! Opt PBE ... CPCM(Methanol)" (no D3BJ) + %method Functional 106 + tda true
#   → 1st optimization cycle: TD-DFT completes successfully
#   → 2nd optimization cycle: CIS module crashes with SIGABRT in CPSCF_Calc_XC
#   → TDA helped the first cycle but LibXC B3LYP is fundamentally unstable
#
# ROOT CAUSE: ORCA 6.1's LibXC interface for B3LYP (functional 106) has an
# intermittent bug in the XC kernel evaluation (CPSCF_Calc_XC) during TD-DFT
# gradient calculations. It crashes unpredictably — sometimes on the 1st cycle,
# sometimes after several cycles. The ORCA 6.1 manual does NOT document any
# "third functional derivative" restriction for B3LYP, suggesting this is a
# bug, not a documented limitation.
#
# RESOLUTION: Switched to CAM-B3LYP for the entire cascade. CAM-B3LYP has
# native analytical TD-DFT gradient support in ORCA 6.1 without any workarounds.
#===============================================================================
#
# ===== ARCHIVED: Original workaround notes (kept for reference) =====
#
# The PBE decoy trick: "! Opt PBE ..." passes ORCA input validation
# (PBE has native third derivatives). %method Functional 106 overrides
# PBE with LibXC's B3LYP at runtime.
#
# D3BJ pitfall: PBE decoy loads PBE's D3BJ parameters. D3 override
# keywords (D3s6/s8/a1/a2) are NOT valid in ORCA 6.1 %method block.
#
# TDA: tda true is needed for stability but does NOT fully resolve the
# intermittent LibXC B3LYP crash.
#
#===============================================================================
# KEYWORDS EXPLAINED:
#   Opt              Geometry optimization (on the excited state PES)
#   PBE              Decoy functional — overridden by %method Functional 106
#   RIJCOSX          RI-J + COSX for computational efficiency
#   6-31G(d)         Basis set (must match S₀ calculation)
#   D3BJ             Dispersion correction
#   CPCM(Methanol)   Solvent model (must match S₀)
#   TightOpt/TightScf Tighter convergence for reliable excited state geometry
#   nroots 5         Compute 5 lowest excited states
#   iroot 1          Optimize geometry on the 1st excited state (S₁)
#   Functional 106   LibXC functional ID for B3LYP
#===============================================================================
# POST-RUN CHECKS:
#   1. grep "ORCA TERMINATED NORMALLY" <out>  → job finished
#   2. grep "HURRAY" <out>                     → optimization converged
#   3. grep "Root   1:" <out>                  → S₁ energy + oscillator strength
#   4. Emission energy E_em = Root 1 energy (eV) × 8065.54 → cm⁻¹
#   5. Oscillator strength f from Root 1 line
#   6. Check <basename>_S1_Opt.xyz exists      → optimized S₁ geometry
#===============================================================================

! Opt PBE RIJCOSX 6-31G(d) CPCM(Methanol)
! TightOpt
! TightScf

%maxcore 3072

%pal
   nprocs 16
end

%method
  Functional 106
end

%tddft
  nroots 5
  iroot 1
  tda   true
end

* xyz 1 1
  <INSERT S₀ OPTIMIZED GEOMETRY HERE — from S₀ Opt .xyz file>
*